It is Thursday evening, and I am at the sports hall.
I play badminton here every week.
I am playing a match against another woman from the club.
The match is very exciting and close.
We are playing for the very last point.
She hits the shuttlecock hard.
It flies fast over the net and over towards me.
I take a big step across the court to reach it.
I swing my racket with all my power.
I hit the shuttlecock perfectly.
It lands right on the white line.
The point is mine, and I win the match.
My opponent smiles across the net and says, "Good match!"
"Thank you very much, that was a difficult point," I reply.
I stand by the net for a bit to catch my breath.
I am sweating a lot and need a break.
I find my red water bottle in the bag.
I drink a lot of cold water.
It is great to use my body after a long day at the office.
